<template>
  <section>
    <h2 class="pdx-txt-heading section-heading">Multiple Items</h2>
    <p class="pdx-txt-small pdx-ink-muted">Consecutive accordion items with merged borders. Wrap in <code>.pdx-accordion-group</code>.</p>

    <div class="pdx-accordion-group">
      <details class="pdx-accordion">
        <summary>Getting Started</summary>
        <div class="pdx-accordion-body">
          Install the framework with <code>npm i @pdxui/framework</code> and create your
          first component with <code>pdx new my-app</code>. The CLI scaffolds a complete
          project with routing, state management, and dev server.
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="pdx-accordion">
        <summary>Component Model</summary>
        <div class="pdx-accordion-body">
          Components are authored as <code>.pdx</code> single-file components with template,
          script, and style blocks. The compiler transforms decorators like <code>@prop</code>
          and <code>$signal</code> into optimized runtime code.
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="pdx-accordion">
        <summary>Styling</summary>
        <div class="pdx-accordion-body">
          Pragmatic CSS provides semantic utility classes with <code>pdx-</code> prefix.
          Styles are scoped by default. The design system includes tokens for colors,
          spacing, typography, and responsive breakpoints.
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>

